Basic relationship:
a: opposite side, b: adjacent side, c: hypotenuse
$math{sin v = a/c, cos v = b/c, tan v = a/b, cot v = b/a}
$math{arcsin a/c = v [-\pi/2, \pi/2], arccos b/c = v [0, \pi], arctan a/b = v [-\pi/2, \pi/2], arccot b/a = v [-\pi/2, \pi/2]}

Trigonometric functions are not injective, need to restrict the function for a new one to make them injective
$math{\arcsin(a/c) = v (from f(x)=(sin(x):-\pi/2<=x<=\pi/2))}
$math{arccos b/c = v (from f(x)=(cos(x):0<=x<=\pi))}
$math{arctan a/b = v (from f(x)=(tan(x):-\pi/2<x<\pi/2))}
$math{arccot b/a = v (from f(x)=(cot(x):-\pi/2<x<\pi/2))}

Using variable substitute
$math{cos(s+t)+cos(s-t)=2cos(s)cos(t)}
$math{x=s+t, y=s-t => s=(x+y)/2, t=(x-y)/2 => cos(x)+cos(y)=cos((x+y)/2)cos((x-y)/2)}

$math{A + B + C = 180\degree}
$math{sin(A) + sin(B) + sin(C) = 4cos(1/2A)cos(1/2B)cos(1/2C)}
$math{cos(A) + cos(B) + cos(C) = 4sin(1/2A)sin(1/2B)sin(1/2C) + 1}
$math{sin(A)^2 + sin(B)^2 + sin(C)^2 = 2*cos(A)*cos(B)*cos(C) + 2}

$math{(b - c)/a = sin(1/2*(B - C))/cos(1/2A)}
$math{(c - a)/b = sin(1/2(C - A))/cos(1/2B)}
$math{(a - b)/c = sin(1/2(A - B))/cos(1/2*C)}

$math{(b + c)/a = cos(1/2*(B - C))/sin(1/2A)}
$math{(a + b)/c = cos(1/2(A - B))/sin(1/2C)}
$math{(c + a)/b = cos(1/2(C - A))/sin(1/2*B)}

$math{sin(1/2*A) = sqrt(((s - b)(s - c))/(b*c))}
$math{sin(1/2*B) = sqrt(((s - a)(s - c))/(a*c))}
$math{sin(1/2*C) = sqrt(((s - a)(s - b))/(a*b))}

$math{cos(1/2*A) = sqrt((s(s - a))/(b*c))}
$math{cos(1/2*B) = sqrt((s(s - b))/(a*c))}
$math{cos(1/2*C) = sqrt((s(s - c))/(a*b))}

$math{tan(1/2*A) = r/(s - a)}
$math{tan(1/2*B) = r/(s - b)}
$math{tan(1/2*C) = r/(s - c)}

Use reduction formula to equivalent domain
$math{sin(v)=sin(A)}
$math{cos(v)=cos(A)}
$math{tan(v)=tan(A)}

$math{a*sin(kx+b)+c=d => a*sin(kx+b)=d-c => sin(kx+b)=(d-c)/a}
$math{=(1)=> kx+b=arcsin((d-c)/a)+2\pi*n => x = (arcsin((d-c)/a)-b+2\pi*n)/k}
$math{=(2)=> kx+b=\pi-arcsin((d-c)/a)+2\pi*n => x = (\pi-arcsin((d-c)/a)-b+2\pi*n)/k}

$math{a*cos(kx+b)+c=d => a*cos(kx+b)=d-c => cos(kx+b)=(d-c)/a}
$math{=(1)=> kx+b=arccos((d-c)/a)+2\pi*n => x = (arccos((d-c)/a)-b+2\pi*n)/k}
$math{=(2)=> kx+b=-arccos((d-c)/a)+2\pi*n => x = (-arccos((d-c)/a)-b+2\pi*n)/k}
$math{[=(2')=> kx+b=2*\pi-arccos((d-c)/a)+2\pi*n => x = (-arccos((d-c)/a)-b+2\pi*n)/k]}

Presetted values:
$math{A=3, B=4, C=5, D=3, \ph=arccos(3/5)}
$math{A=2, B=5, C=sqrt(29), D=-4, \ph=arccos(2/sqrt(29))}
$math{A=5, B=-21, C=13, D=13, \ph=arccos(5/13)}
$math{A=1/3, B=2sqrt(2)/3, C=1, D=1/sqrt(2), \ph=arccos(1/3)}
